Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:23:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 420/488] [DS4.1] Rejection sampler's block verification in
 TileLang

Production's verification (one-hot drafts, block verification, FP32
draws, no watermark) runs as TileLang kernels, the contract of the
Triton kernels bit for bit: the local logits statistics, the cumulative
log-probabilities and the rejection fused into one verify kernel, and
the resample. The arithmetic follows Triton 3.7's PTX and SASS for
sm_121a, including the FMA LLVM fuses into the first level of a row's
log-sum-exp reduction (lane 0, which stores, is the contract). Every
other configuration stays on the Triton kernels.
